	{ version = "v0.4.1.1", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Changed", [6] = "Fixed", [8] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aEvery profession in Craft|r: all 12 (Alchemy, Blacksmithing, Enchanting, Engineering, Herbalism, Leatherworking, Mining, Skinning, Tailoring, Cooking, First Aid, Fishing) with every recipe, from the client's own data tables (WoW Forever 1.60.1.70888). No profession window needs opening; a tab you show still replaces its list with the game's own.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA profession dropdown|r replaces the buttons: yours are starred and listed first, then the primary professions, then the secondary.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAll the priced crafts, paged|r, by profit per craft (was the Top 10). Crafts that can't be priced or aren't listed stay named under the list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aTotal|r column: profit per craft x how many you can make (follows Count the bank).",
		"|cff6e2c0aHarvest|r: Herbalism, Mining, Skinning and Fishing get a Crafts | Harvest switch: every herb, ore and stone, hide and raw fish or meat, with its AH lowest, how many are listed, its vendor price, what you have and its 7-day change.",
		"|cff6e2c0aKnown only works for every profession|r (Cooking and First Aid too): each recipe is asked of the game, no window needed.",
		"|cff6e2c0aTop 10|r counts the hours with a full scan, not the scans (history keeps one point an hour, so two scans in one hour count once), and says when your next full scan counts. Its message no longer sits on top of the Rising and Falling headers.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.4.1", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "New", [6] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aCraft|r (AH Market): the Top 10 crafts of each profession by profit at the Auction House shown: craft cost, sell price (the lowest buyout, no undercut), profit per item and margin, how many are listed, a star on the recipes you know and how many you can make. Every item shows its icon and the game's tooltip, with each reagent's cost under it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRecipes come from the game|r: open a profession window once (any character) and Valhalla keeps its whole list, learned or not, for every character. Reagents and outputs are always read from the game. A few recipe IDs are bundled for the professions not opened yet; a fuller bundled list will follow.",
		"|cff6e2c0aCosts|r: each reagent at the cheaper of the AH's lowest and a merchant you've visited. Reagents: Market (all bought), Owned free (what's in your bags, or bags + bank, costs nothing) or Owned: vendor (at its vendor value). Known only shows just your recipes.",
		"The sale is less the house's cut (5%, 15% at Booty Bay, Gadgetzan and Everlook). The deposit isn't taken off: the game gives it back when the item sells (the tooltip shows it, estimated).",
		"A craft with a reagent nobody prices, or whose item isn't listed, isn't ranked: it's named under the Top 10 (your next quick scan asks about them). Enchants and bind-on-pickup items are skipped.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.4.0.2", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [3] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aNo more freeze opening My items or Scan results|r: v0.4.0.1 could build the list dozens of times over when it first measured the window, leaving copies drawn over each other (rows doubled, History's box and the Count and Range rows overlapping, the game slow). Each list is now built once, and resizing the window only lays out its own rows again.",
		"Changing to another view hides every other one, so nothing is left drawn underneath.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.4.0.1", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Changed", [5] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aMy items and Scan results go through everything|r: page buttons under the list (first, back, next, last) with Page x of y and which items are shown. The mouse wheel turns a page. Changing bags/bank, the house, the search or the sort goes back to page 1.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAs many rows as the window fits|r (6 to 20): more in the full-screen map, no overlap in the small one.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe round icon shows the whole hall|r: the gable, both dragon heads and the doors, in the window's portrait and on the minimap button.",
		"History draws every scan's point (one an hour at most): it needs no number of scans. Top 10 still needs 3 full scans.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.4.0", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "New", [7] = "Changed", [9] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aAH Market|r: prices from your own scans at the Auction House. |cff6e2c0aScan|r is on Valhalla's list beside the AH: a full scan of the whole market (about 15 seconds, read a little each frame so the game doesn't stall) when its 15 minutes are up, else a quick scan of your items (shopping list, bags, bank). The button turns into Stop with a bar; minimized, right-click the small button. It only reads prices: nothing is posted, bid or bought.",
		"|cff6e2c0aTop 10|r rising and falling over 7 days (needs 3 full scans): the median lowest price of the second half of the window against the first, with a small sparkline.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMy items|r: everything in your bags (or bags + bank), its vendor price against the AH's lowest after the cut (5%, 15% at Booty Bay, Gadgetzan and Everlook), and the better of the two.",
		"|cff6e2c0aHistory|r: one item's lowest price over a day or a week (lines or bars, Settings' graph style). |cff6e2c0aScan results|r: every item of the last full scan, searchable and sortable by name, lowest, units, auctions or 7-day change.",
		"|cff6e2c0aEvery item shows its icon and the game's own tooltip|r (shift-hover compares gear), with what the AH said under it. Shift-click links it, ctrl-click tries it on, click opens its History, right-click puts it in the Shopping List's builder. Items the game hasn't loaded show their icon at once and their name a moment later. The AH list's items show the tooltip too.",
		"Each Auction House is its own market (Alliance, Horde, neutral). History keeps one point per item an hour (the latest wins), 7 days, at most 3 MB. A full scan cut off by closing the AH saves nothing. Settings > AH Market: scan speed, days kept, history size, the 1c-dump filter (off: the raw lowest price), shift-compare, forget a house.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRun AH check|r moved to /valhalla invest diag ah (the AH list's button is Scan now). /valhalla invest scan scans from chat.",
		"Valhalla's icon is the hall: the AddOn list, the minimap button and the window's portrait.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRestart the game once|r after installing (new files: a /reload doesn't load them). Craft profit (v0.4.1) will need only a /reload.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.5", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [3] = "Changed", [7] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aRun AH check works|r: its button is now on Valhalla's list beside the Auction House (the game never shows the Valhalla window and the Auction House together, so the Settings button could never be pressed). It turns into Stop while the check runs, with its step and a bar; minimized, right-click the small button to run or stop it. Settings keeps the button with a hint, and /valhalla invest diag ah still works.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSettings no longer overlaps|r: each note is as tall as its text at the window's width (measured again when the window is resized). The AH check's long description moved into the button's tooltip.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSettings is its own tab|r, right of Professions. Investments' menu is Smart Vendor, Shopping List and AH Market. /valhalla invest settings and /valhalla tab settings open it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe window is called Valhalla|r, windowed and full screen, and its portrait is Valhalla's icon on every tab.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe other tabs are clean|r: on Investments, Talents, Professions and Settings, the map's breadcrumb, the quest log's search box and the Quests count are covered by the tab's own panel, and Valhalla's map menu is put away (back on Map & Quest Log).",
		"Nothing of the game's window is changed: the title is set again after the game's own, the strip is covered by a panel of Valhalla's.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.4", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "New", [3] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aRun AH check|r (Investments > Settings, at the Auction House, or /valhalla invest diag ah): measures what the coming AH Market can use: how long the full scan takes to answer and to read, how many auctions, whether stackable goods (commodities) are in it and its cooldown, how fast quick price searches answer and how many items one can ask for, whether recipes can be read with the profession window closed or for recipes you don't know, which house this is (faction or neutral), and a deposit sample. It runs a few steps over 1-4 minutes without freezing the game and prints its results; /reload writes them to disk.",
		"|cff6e2c0aIt only reads prices|r: it never posts, bids, buys or cancels, and nothing of the market is stored beyond its few numbers. Closing the Auction House stops it (saved as stopped); /valhalla invest diag stop stops it too. The plain diagnostic now also says which recipes can be read.",
		"A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.3", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Changed", [3] = "New", [4] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aBuying never changes your lists|r: a vendor or Auction House purchase no longer takes anything off a list. Lists change only when you edit or delete them. Each line just shows how many you still need, Done once you have enough, or In the mail for what you bought at the Auction House until you loot it. Undo is for deleting and editing a list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWhat's on your list keeps glowing at vendors|r once you have enough (tagged Done), and stays in the Auction House list (Done) as long as it's on the chosen list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNone|r: the list picker at vendors and the Auction House has None at the top: no list, no highlights, and the AH list says No list selected. None is remembered until you choose a list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aKeep is gone|r from the builder (with nothing ever taken off a list, it had nothing left to do). A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.2", date = "2026-11-10", heads = { [1] = "Changed", [5] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aShopping lists you build and name|r: the Shopping List page now has a builder at the top. Give the list a name (left empty, it's named List 1, List 2, ...), find items by typing part of a name (or shift-click or drop an item into the box: still no stack-split box), Add or Remove them, set how many (- / + or type it; 0 to start) and tick Keep to keep one stocked. Build Shopping List saves it below and clears the builder for the next one.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour lists below|r, each with its items and how many you still need (from your bags and bank, live), what's in the mail, Done or Stocked. Edit puts a list back in the builder (Save List keeps it in its place); Delete removes it, with Undo.",
		"|cff6e2c0aBought it? Only that line comes off|r, and only on the active list (said in chat, with Undo). What you buy at the Auction House stays 'In the mail' until you loot it. Your other lists are left alone; Keep lines stay as a standing target.",
		"|cff6e2c0aChoose the active list at a vendor or the Auction House|r: a small 'List: ...' button above the merchant window and under the AH list's title opens a menu of your lists. The highlights and the AH list follow it at once, and it's remembered. With one list it's chosen for you; with none, the button says to build one and opens the Shopping List.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSmart Vendor is under construction|r (coming soon): what you had on it became one list, \"My List\", the first time you log in with this version, and the old list is kept as it was in your saved data. /valhalla want and unwant now add to and remove from the builder; /valhalla list shows the active list. A /reload is enough after installing (no new files).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.1", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [3] = "New", [9] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aThe window always opens on Map & Quest Log|r (M, L, or anything else opening it), with Investments, Talents and Professions really hidden: in v0.3.0 the last tab's panel could come back over the map. With the window open, on any tab, L closes it, as M does from another tab. The 'open on the last tab' setting is gone.",
		"|cff6e2c0aShift-click into Valhalla's boxes no longer opens the stack-split box|r: when the Smart Vendor box (or another Valhalla box) has the cursor and takes the item, the split box closes again. Anywhere else shift-click is the game's own.",
		"|cff6e2c0aBought it? It comes off your list|r: once you have what you wanted in hand, it's taken off the list and said in chat, with Undo (the button in Investments, or /valhalla undo). Tick |cff6e2c0aKeep|r on a row to keep it stocked instead: hidden while you have enough, back when it's used up.",
		"|cff6e2c0aIn the mail|r: what you buy at the Auction House counts as in the mail (Smart Vendor's Mail column, the Shopping List's In the mail group, the AH list's footer) until it reaches your bags, so it isn't bought twice. The mailbox, when open, says what's really there.",
		"|cff6e2c0aOne-click Search at the Auction House|r: Search puts the name in and presses the AH's own Search button for you, on your click (the game's own search runs). If the game won't allow it, the name is left in the search box: press Enter. The experimental One-click setting is gone.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe AH list minimizes|r: its - leaves a small button at the Auction House's top right with how many items you need; click it to bring the list back. Minimized or not is remembered.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe bank, visible|r: each bank visit says in chat what was counted (items, kinds, tabs; the warband bank too). The bank is noticed by either of the game's two signals, its own first tab is always read, and 'Bank last seen' is under the menu on every Investments page.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDiagnostic buttons|r: Investments > Settings > Run diagnostic (and Run AH check at the Auction House) save what Valhalla sees, the bank above all, and print three lines; then /reload writes it to disk.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRestart the game|r (not just /reload) after installing: this version adds a file (Links.lua), and the game reads its list of files only at start. No new saved file.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.0", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "New", [5] = "Note", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aTabs on the Valhalla window|r: Map & Quest Log (everything as before), Investments, and Talents and Professions (under construction, coming soon). Below the window by default; along the top or as icons down the side in Investments > Settings. /valhalla tab map|invest|talents|professions.",
		"|cff6e2c0aSmart Vendor|r (Investments): mark the reagents, profession materials and gear upgrades you want and how many; Valhalla counts your bags as they change and your bank as it was last seen open, and works out what you still need. /valhalla want <item> [count] [mat|reagent|gear].",
		"|cff6e2c0aShopping List|r: what you still need, by where to buy it (a vendor you've visited, else the Auction House). At a vendor, what you need glows gold with \"need N\"; the rest is greyed but still yours to buy. At the Auction House, your list opens beside it with a Search button per item. Valhalla never buys for you.",
		"|cff6e2c0a/valhalla invest diag|r checks what this client offers for the coming Auction House market (Phase C) and saves it (/reload to write it to disk). /valhalla invest off turns the tabs and Investments off.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRestart the game|r (not just /reload) after installing: Investments keeps its data in a new saved file, ValhallaInvestDB.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.2.2", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "New", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aQuests with something to do here show here|r: a quest from another zone that has a real objective marker on this zone's map (or a capital's surrounding zone's) is listed in Quests, and once it's ready, a turn-in marker here puts it in Ready to Turn In. \"Travel this way\" waypoints, map indicators and other maps' pins don't count, and dungeon quests stay in their dungeon. Once its marker here is gone it leaves (after a second look, never in combat or in flight).",
		"|cff6e2c0aPins in the quest log|r: the same pin left of each quest's icon in the quest log, the same as on All Objectives: pin or unpin in either and both follow.",
		"|cff6e2c0a/valhalla objectives why|r says when a quest is listed for its marker here, and why a marker doesn't count.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.2.1", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", [4] = "New", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aQuests from other zones no longer leak in|r: a quest's zone header in the quest log decides where it's listed (\"Excavation Site: Wetlands\" counts as Wetlands). The game's \"travel this way\" and map-indicator pins no longer pull in Duskwood quests in Stormwind or Wetlands quests in Ironforge, in Quests or in Ready to Turn In.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReady to Turn In drops unpinned quests from other zones|r, and every ready quest leaves the Quests list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReady to Turn In's quest icon is the game's own|r, the same size and look as the Quests list's: click to select the quest, click again to clear it. Its collapse button is the Quests header's.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon quests only in their dungeon|r: outside, they're hidden unless pinned; inside a dungeon only its own quests (and pinned ones) are listed.",
		"|cff6e2c0a/valhalla objectives why [questID]|r tells you where Valhalla thinks you are and why each quest is listed or not.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.2.0", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "New", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aAll Objectives by zone|r: the Quests section lists this zone's quests (in a capital, the city's and its surrounding zone's), lowest level first. It changes only once you've landed or arrived, never in combat.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReady to Turn In|r: a section of its own at the bottom of All Objectives for this zone's quests that are ready to hand in. Click one to select it and open it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aPins|r: the pin left of a quest keeps it listed in every zone. Off by default; saved per character.",
		"|cff6e2c0aTurn it off any time|r with /valhalla objectives off (or in Options): the game's own tracking comes back, with the quests Valhalla untracked tracked again.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.1.0", date = "2026-11-09", heads = { [1] = "New", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aValhalla|r: Odysseaus's own fork of OpenMap v0.8.2 by OpenMap contributors (MIT). Its own name, settings (ValhallaDB), /valhalla and /vh, key bindings and windows. The notes below are OpenMap's.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.2", date = "2026-11-08", heads = { [1] = "Improved", [2] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aPanning no longer hitches|r: the map set up to 300 textures' files in a single frame where a pan brought new ground into view, and each set is a load and an upload, so that frame showed as a hitch of about 35 ms. It sets 60 a frame now; the art still fades in, a few frames later.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map no longer stalls a moment after it opens|r: since 0.8.0 OpenMap keeps the map's art loaded while it's closed, then let go of it all in one frame a second into the opening, which the game unloaded at once (about a second's freeze). It now lets go of it a little at a time.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZooming in notch by notch is smooth again|r: since 0.8.1 the blur came back all at once each time the map stopped, one long frame the next wheel notch landed on. It now waits out a pause between notches and comes back a few zones a frame. Questie's mob paths are worked out once the map stops, not on every frame of a zoom.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.1", date = "2026-11-08", heads = { [1] = "New", [3] = "Improved", [7] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's mob paths on the stitched map|r, drawn over the art for the zones near the view as you zoom in (Questie's own were under the art, and only on the zone's own map).",
		"|cff6e2c0aDarkening colour|r (Options, under Darkening): the colour unexplored areas are darkened with, picked with the game's colour picker; |cff6e2c0aDefault colour|r brings back the dark one.",
		"|cff6e2c0aZooming is about four times smoother|r: OpenMap no longer lays out its hidden icons and its blur on every frame of a zoom (the blur comes back a moment after you stop). Found and measured by Peendars.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters are easier to see on the map|r: bigger, with a dark outline, and the ones you haven't learned are no longer half see-through (they were lost on the parchment).",
		"|cff6e2c0aCtrl-click drops a pin can be turned off|r (Options, and the menu's More tab): with Map Pin Enhanced a Ctrl-click dropped two pins, its own and OpenMap's. Off, the menu's Drop a pin still works.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe Drowned City's map is Santiago Reyes's updated version|r, which names more of its places (the Eternal Amphitheater and the Abyssal Dais).",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon and cave maps show in every language|r: on the Latin American Spanish, Russian and Italian clients every dungeon map and Blizzard cave map was solid green squares, as the game doesn't have their art for those languages. OpenMap now brings that art itself. Found and first fixed by RADD95 (OpenMap TextureFix): with this version that addon isn't needed. (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aZone names in your client's language|r: on every client but English, the zones' prebuilt art lettered their English names over the map. Other languages now draw the zones from the client's own art (zooming is a little slower there, as with that art turned off).",
		"|cff6e2c0aQuestie's icons show the first time you open the map|r: after a login they could be missing until the map was closed and opened again (Questie was still setting up when OpenMap looked).",
		"|cff6e2c0aZygor's waypoint shows on the stitched map|r, in the right place and over the art (Zygor uses its own renamed copy of HereBeDragons, which OpenMap didn't know). Traced by robnoord.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour class's trainers are found on every language's client|r: on a French client (and the other non-English ones) every class trainer showed as a profession trainer.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAn NPC who walks about shows once on the map|r: Girl with Puppies in Orgrimmar had a vendor icon at every point of her walk, dozens over the city. An NPC with many spawns in one zone (with Vendors and the other townsfolk on) now has one icon, in the middle of where it walks. Fixed by diegodiaz1256.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opened on Zephras Isle shows Zephras Isle|r, as its airship opens it: it showed the stitched world with no one on it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo friends dot or badge for yourself|r: with Share where you are on, you could show on your own map as a guild member (the guild's roster can spell your realm differently).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opens at once inside a dungeon|r: each opening loaded the dungeon's map art again, a second or two (longer in dungeons with many floors, whose Floors tab shows every floor). OpenMap now keeps the art of the dungeon you're in loaded, as it does the world map's.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.8.0-beta", date = "2026-11-07", heads = { [1] = "New", [3] = "Improved", [5] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aFriends and guild on the map|r (Options: Friends and guild): your guild members and friends on your realm who are online show on the stitched map, a badge on the zone each is in with who's there. Those who use OpenMap and turn on |cff6e2c0aShare where you are|r show as a class-coloured dot where they stand, updated every few seconds while they move. The map asks once whether to share; it's off unless you say yes, goes only to your guild and your friends, and never from inside a dungeon, raid or battleground.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMaps of The Drowned City, Krol'dok Stronghold and Shaper's Terrace|r, drawn by Santiago Reyes and used with his permission (credited on the map, as his other dungeon maps are).",
		"|cff6e2c0aA new OpenMap icon, drawn by zloyeb|r: a map scroll in a gold ring, in the AddOns list, on the minimap button, in the map's menu and its portrait (it borrowed the game's Eastern Kingdoms icon).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap is back on GitHub|r, at github.com/openmap-world/openmap: Report a problem opens a report there again, and What's new and the AddOns list link to it.",
		"|cff6e2c0a\"Center on player, keep zoom\" opens at your zoom straight away|r: having moved since the map closed, it opened on the zone's whole map for a moment and then jumped to the zoom kept.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opens with its art already there|r: the game let go of the map's art while it was closed, and each opening loaded it again (blank parchment for a moment). OpenMap now keeps it loaded while the map is closed; /openmap warm turns that off.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map closes in combat again|r: with the map open as a fight started, neither Escape nor M closed it (since 0.7.0). The windowed map no longer stays open beside an NPC's window, which is what blocked it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters you haven't learned show as not learned|r: every one showed as learned, as WoW Forever reports them all as found. OpenMap now goes by the ones a flight master shows you've learned: what it remembered is forgotten once and counted again at the next flight master you talk to.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map window can't go above the top of the screen|r, where its title bar couldn't be grabbed to bring it back. /openmap reset puts the window back to its size and place.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDun Morogh stays Dun Morogh near Ironforge|r: around Kharanos, panning or zooming switched the map to Ironforge's and a click zoomed into the city. A city's map now takes over only in its middle, and its zone comes first when you click your way in.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe OpenMap menu fits a short screen|r: on a TV at a big UI scale the Look tab ran off the bottom.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters are named in your own language|r: on a client that isn't English, the map's flight masters kept the game's tables' English names (hovering one said \"Stormwind, Elwynn\" while the flight master in game names it in your language). They're now named as the game names them, and a flight's measured time is found again on a route (the times were keyed by the English names).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map opened inside a dungeon shows that dungeon's map|r (Ragefire Chasm, Deadmines ...): it showed the world map with no one on it, as WoW Forever has no map of its dungeons. Its map only opened from the entrance on the world map.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.5-beta", date = "2026-10-23", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map's art is there at once when you open it|r: since 0.7.4 the zones showed blank parchment for a moment each time the map opened.",
		"|cff6e2c0aClicking a quest on the map keeps the map as it is|r: the quest is tracked and the map zooms in on it, full screen or windowed. It opened the quest's details, which Blizzard shows in the windowed map, so a full-screen map left full screen. With the quest log open beside the map, its details show there too.",
		"|cff6e2c0aHiding your pins hides their drawings too|r (the menu's Pins, right-clicked): what you drew on a pin stayed on the map without it.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.4-beta", date = "2026-10-23", heads = { [1] = "New", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aChat over the full-screen map|r (the menu's Look tab, and Options): the chat windows stay on show over the map while it's full screen, to keep talking while you look. Off unless you turn it on (a player's request).",
		"|cff6e2c0aFaster to load|r: only your language's translations are read (the other nine were a quarter of OpenMap's code), and its look through every addon's map icons for combat waits till you're in the world, not the loading screen (a player's report: half a second more load time).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe zones' detail comes in sooner|r when the map first opens up close: it took a couple of seconds after a login or reload.",
		"|cff6e2c0a/openmap status says what loading costs|r: OpenMap's files, the login, the map's setup and building the map (a player found it added load time: this shows where).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.3-beta", date = "2026-10-22", heads = { [1] = "New", [5] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aKey bindings|r (the game's Keybindings > OpenMap): Find me, Drop a pin, Pins, Quill, Quest log and the map's menu, each opening the map first if it's closed (players' requests).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe quill draws on dungeons' maps|r: with a dungeon's map up, what you draw goes on its picture and is kept with that dungeon, not on the world map behind it (a player's request).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOnly places you've found|r (the menu's On the map tab, under Places): dungeon entrances, docks and zeppelin towers once you've explored where they are, flight masters once you've learned them. Off unless you turn it on (a player's request).",
		"|cff6e2c0aTownsfolk from another addon's NPC database|r: an addon with a database in Questie's shape can give it to OpenMap (OpenMapAPI.RegisterTownsfolkProvider, docs/api.md), so townsfolk and rare mobs show without Questie (a player's request).",
		"|cff6e2c0aSmooth zooming at any Take colour out|r: the zones' fast pre-drawn art was only used at the setting's default (10%); at any other, every zone was drawn from its hundreds of pieces and the frame rate dropped as their detail came in. It's now used at every setting.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFull screen stays full screen|r, and the quest log you closed stays closed, the next time the map opens: it went back to the window and the quest log each time (a player's report).",
		"|cff6e2c0aImproves performance|r under Fade icons while zooming no longer stays on show over the menu's other tabs (a player's report).",
		"|cff6e2c0aRiverglades and Zephras Isle show their levels|r on the zone hover (35-45 and 1-12, from the Warcraft Wiki; a player's report).",
	} },
}
